{"id":"CQ-001","category":"code_quality","criterion":"test_coverage","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":"head/evals/graders/recall-vs-defects.sh","line":74,"code_snippet":"r'|(?:(?<![A-Za-z0-9_./:])(?:head|base)|(?<![A-Za-z0-9_./:])):(?P<bare>' + RNG + r')(?![A-Za-z0-9])')","reasoning_trace":"Traced review text (untrusted model output) into the 1.1.0 CITE regex. The bare `:N` alternative's negative lookbehind rejects only word/path characters and a colon, so `\"`, `'`, `}`, `]`, `)` and `*` pass. Every graded review ends with a LOA-VERDICT trailer whose `\"counts\":{\"critical\":0,\"high\":0,\"medium\":7,...}` therefore yields bare citations 0,0,7,0 bound to the last cited path. Reproduced on head with a synthetic manifest: `c.sh:100` + trailer `\"medium\":7` detects a defect anchored at c.sh:7 (6 citations); `d.sh:300 … {\"line\":1,\"count\":2}` detects d.sh:2; an all-zero trailer detects any defect anchored within 0..3 of the last cited file. The base 1.0.0 parser credits none of these (1 citation).","finding":"Bare `:N` citation alternative binds JSON values (including every review's own LOA-VERDICT trailer counts) to the last cited file, over-reporting recall in the instrument the Task 4.8 replay A/B rule depends on","critique":"A measuring instrument changed by regex needs adversarial inputs drawn from the documents it will score. The header contract (lines 17-21) promises a `:N` glued to a word or number credits nothing, but the implementation only excludes identifier characters.","remediation":"Require whitespace, start-of-text, a backtick or an opening paren before the bare colon: replace the empty-lookbehind branch with `(?:^|(?<=[\\s`(]))` and extend the lookbehind before `head|base` the same way; add RG cases where the trailer count equals a planted anchor and where inline JSON follows a citation, asserting zero detections; bump grader_version to 1.1.1 and re-run the replay A/B that drove the Task 4.8 revert.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-185 ht